  "body": "Seen once in a whole `go test -count=1 ./internal/library ./internal/gui` run on mote, at ce2a59daa plus the MCP command-variables change (which leaves a server with no `$`/`~` in its command untouched: `launchCmd` returns it as is). It passed 10 of 10 run alone (`-run 'TestRunServerAsks|TestRun' -count=10`).\n\n```\n--- FAIL: TestRunServerAsks (0.02s)\n    mcp_run_test.go:278: asked: {\"id\":5,\"jsonrpc\":\"2.0\",\"result\":{\"content\":[{\"text\":\"roots \",\"type\":\"text\"}]}}\n```\n\nThe first thing on the call's stream was the call's own reply (`roots ` with nothing after it), not the server's `roots/list` request (id 77). So the fake server seems to have answered the tool call before its ask reached the stream, or the ask was sent to another stream. That looks like an ordering assumption in the run session or the fixture, not load. Not yet looked into.\n",
