   "body": "The ordering race is fixed on [the fork branch](https://github.com/skygunner/magpie/tree/fix/5433-register-mcp-stream-before-send), commit [5acae7bee](https://github.com/skygunner/magpie/commit/5acae7bee5cd87d816bd9ca8abcd24b9b3a82e94), based on `ed0ab567`.\n\n`ServeRun` now registers the call's SSE stream before sending its request to the child. Previously an immediate `roots/list` could arrive before that stream existed: it was rejected when no stream was open, or delivered to an older session stream. The new stream is closed on every return, including a failed send.\n\nA temporary channel barrier reproduced the exact first reply `roots ` on the base, and the same barrier passes with the fix. The permanent HTTP/subprocess regression holds the pipe write until the request is delivered and deterministically catches delivery to an older stream on the old ordering. The original `TestRunServerAsks` assertion is unchanged. Parent `TestRun*` checks passed under `-race`; library vet, formatting and the full `nogui` build passed.\n\nThe older stream in the regression is opened through the session registry, rather than an HTTP GET. Independent overlapping POSTs retain the existing newest-stream policy. Full-suite and cross-platform runtime checks were not run. AI-assisted implementation and review.",
